# Twitter API Core

Lux provides transport-neutral Twitter/X API request planning helpers for OAuth
2.0 PKCE, tweet management, user interactions, media upload, rate limits, and
error classification.

## OAuth 2.0 PKCE

```elixir
alias Lux.Integrations.Twitter.Client

pkce = Client.pkce_pair("abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz1234567890")

Client.authorization_url(%{
  client_id: "client-1",
  redirect_uri: "https://example.com/callback",
  state: "state-1",
  code_verifier: pkce.verifier
})
```

Exchange a code or refresh token:

```elixir
Client.token_request(:authorization_code, %{
  code: "code-1",
  redirect_uri: "https://example.com/callback",
  client_id: "client-1",
  code_verifier: pkce.verifier
})

Client.token_request(:refresh_token, %{
  refresh_token: "refresh-1",
  client_id: "client-1"
})
```

## Tweets

```elixir
Client.tweet_request(:create, %{
  text: "hello",
  reply_to_tweet_id: "parent-1",
  quote_tweet_id: "quote-1",
  media_ids: ["media-1"],
  access_token: "token"
})

Client.tweet_request(:delete, %{tweet_id: "tweet-1"})

Client.tweet_request(:lookup, %{
  tweet_id: "tweet-1",
  tweet_fields: ["created_at", "public_metrics"]
})
```

## Users

```elixir
Client.user_request(:me, %{user_fields: ["username"]})
Client.user_request(:lookup, %{user_id: "user-1"})
Client.user_request(:follow, %{user_id: "user-1", target_user_id: "user-2"})
Client.user_request(:unfollow, %{user_id: "user-1", target_user_id: "user-2"})
```

## Media Upload

```elixir
Client.media_upload_request(:init, %{
  total_bytes: 1024,
  media_type: "image/png",
  media_category: "tweet_image"
})

Client.media_upload_request(:append, %{
  media_id: "media-1",
  segment_index: 0,
  media_data: "base64"
})

Client.media_upload_request(:finalize, %{media_id: "media-1"})
```

## Rate Limits and Errors

```elixir
Client.rate_limit(%{
  "x-rate-limit-limit" => "300",
  "x-rate-limit-remaining" => "0",
  "x-rate-limit-reset" => "1800"
})

Client.classify_error(429, %{"detail" => "Too Many Requests"})
```

Each helper returns a request plan with method, URL, headers, and payload. The
caller decides which HTTP adapter, token store, and retry loop to use.
